# goose-cli-video-transcription-recipe — project hints

## what this is

pipeline repo for video + podcast transcription. scripts run on rocm-aibox against
~/video-transcripts/ as the data dir. recipes live in recipes/.

## recipes (use /recipe to invoke)

- `intake.yaml` — bulk front door: @handle, playlist url, file of urls, or single url.
  runs yt-dlp --flat-playlist to enumerate real urls, dedupes against existing
  status.json, dispatches --parallel 2. use this for any "transcribe all videos from
  channel/playlist" request. supports --dry-run to enumerate without dispatching.
- `video-transcription-local.yaml` — single-url pipeline (media-extract → whisper → instella-vl → tighten → narrative)
- `tidy.yaml` — retention sweep over ~/video-transcripts/
- `goose-cli-tutor.yaml` — walks a goose-cli principle using qdrant corpus first

## anti-hallucination rule

NEVER enumerate, list, or guess video URLs or titles from memory or training data.
YouTube URLs change, video IDs are opaque, and any list you produce without running
yt-dlp will contain fabricated IDs and dates.

when asked to transcribe videos from a channel or playlist:
1. ask the user to confirm they want --dry-run first or want to dispatch for real
2. run: `python3 scripts/intake.py '<source>' --dry-run`
   where <source> is the url or @handle the user gave you
3. show the enumerated urls from the manifest, confirm with user, then dispatch without --dry-run

never fabricate urls. if you cannot run yt-dlp, say so and ask the user to run it directly.

## correct invocation pattern

```
# dry-run first (enumerate only, no dispatch)
python3 ~/code/projects/goose-cli-video-transcription-recipe/scripts/intake.py \
  '@goose-oss' --dry-run --label goose-oss

# then real run
python3 ~/code/projects/goose-cli-video-transcription-recipe/scripts/intake.py \
  '@goose-oss' --parallel 2 --label goose-oss
```

or via recipe:
```
/recipe intake.yaml source=@goose-oss dry_run_flag=--dry-run
```
